														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2774701">
									

<p>This one isn't working for me. The various logs are a little too disparate and seemingly random to form a coherent picture I would find it to be an improvement, actually, for there to be a unanimous welcoming of the people-napping. Both the first transcript and the running-in-place seem like they're working against the concept, to me at least. On that note, the running excerpt seems cartoonish. I get what you were going for, and the attempt to translate their experience to an outside perspective is commendable, but it doesn't leave the right impression.</p>
<p>You could stand to push the apathy towards the affected further, and their withdrawal that drives them to this thing. The meta-speak is a little insubstantial, and I do wish there was more to it than a couple smiley-faces. I had high hopes that I was going to walk away unsettled based off the description, but it didn't move me in any way.</p>

							</div>

								
					
